  "notes": [
    "Total verified: 64 districts; per-division counts identical in two independent National Portal datasets (district-portal directory and BBS-coded geo API).",
    "name_en = English title of each official district portal (the \"District\" suffix removed). Current spellings used there: Chattogram, Cumilla, Jashore, Bogura, Barishal, Jhalakathi (not Jhalokati), Kishoreganj, Moulvibazar, Netrokona, Chapainawabganj.",
    "Cox's Bazar: the portal title reads \"Coxsbazar District\" (domain-style); the geo API and the district portal body text use \"Cox's Bazar\", so that form is used (slug coxs-bazar).",
    "Khagrachhari/Khagrachari: the portal title uses \"Khagrachari\" (used here, slug khagrachari). The domain khagrachhari.gov.bd and the geo API use \"Khagrachhari\". Both spellings appear on official pages.",
    "Older spellings still in the government geo API (not used): Barisal, Chittagong, Comilla, Jessore, Bogra, Jhalokati, Kishoregonj, Maulvibazar, Netrakona, Chapai Nababganj.",
    "Bangla names come from the district-portal directory. Variants: Rangamati is titled \"রাঙ্গামাটি পার্বত্য জেলা\" (hill district), stored as রাঙ্গামাটি; the geo API writes মুন্সিগঞ্জ (portal: মুন্সীগঞ্জ) and চাঁপাই নাবাবগঞ্জ (portal: চাঁপাইনবাবগঞ্জ).",
    "Division slugs map as follows: the API lists Barisal and Chittagong, stored here as barishal and chattogram (the division portals use these spellings in their English titles). mymensinghdiv.gov.bd returned HTTP 503 during the check, but the same Mymensingh data came from the national API.",
    "bangladesh.gov.bd pages were not needed directly; BBS was not consulted, and the BBS district codes appear only in the geo API."
